    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43150" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sculptĭlis</span></b> , e, adj.
		sculpo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>formed</i> or <i>produced by
			carving</i>, <i>graving</i>, etc., <i>sculptile</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opus dentis Numidae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					P. 4, 9, 28</span></i>
			: forma in aere, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ.</span>
			10, 266. —<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sculptĭle</span></b> , is,
				n., <i>a carved image</i>, <i>statue</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Judic. 17,
				3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sculptilia deorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 1
					Macc. 5, 68</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deos et sculptilia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Dan. 11, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
